    {
      "name": "Protect Backup Performance Degradation",
      "definition": "Calls addressing severe backup throughput drops, extended backup windows, API failures, or scheduler capacity limits in Aegis Protect.",
      "distinguishing": "Specifically involves backup performance bottlenecks and job failures in Aegis Protect, distinct from Detect pipeline outages.",
      "owner": "support lead",
      "actionable_because": "Support leads can develop escalation playbooks for agent version incompatibilities and coordinate with infrastructure teams on job throttling and workarounds.",
      "meeting_ids": [
        "13B60D",
        "51360A",
        "5ADCF8"
      ],
      "evidence": [
        {
          "meeting_id": "13B60D",
          "quote": "Our nightly backup jobs are taking, uh, somewhere between four and six hours to complete. They used to finish in under ninety minutes. This started maybe three weeks ago, and it's just... it's not getting better."
        },
        {
          "meeting_id": "51360A",
          "quote": "So we have our EHR system — it's a custom-built platform — integrated with Aegis Protect through your REST API, and starting Sunday we started getting 503 errors on the backup initiation endpoint. Specifically the... um, it's the /v2/backup/jobs/create endpoint."
        },
        {
          "meeting_id": "5ADCF8",
          "quote": "Throughput started degrading at around the 60% load mark, and by the time we hit full simulated load we were seeing backup job queue times spike to like — I think the worst number was 47 minutes for a job that should complete in under five."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Identity Configuration and Deployment",
      "definition": "Calls involving the implementation, roadmap planning, or technical configuration of Aegis Identity features like SSO, SCIM provisioning, and MFA policies.",
      "distinguishing": "Focuses specifically on IAM setups, directory integrations, and user authentication workflows, rather than threat monitoring or backup jobs.",
      "owner": "product manager",
      "actionable_because": "Product managers can prioritize self-serve attribute mapping UIs, adaptive MFA policies, and streamlined SCIM setup to reduce implementation friction.",
      "meeting_ids": [
        "4B7D41",
        "632514",
        "A55CCD",
        "D2AE7F"
      ],
      "evidence": [
        {
          "meeting_id": "632514",
          "quote": "So let me just go through what we did complete — the SCIM provisioning bug fixes, that was four story points. The SSO metadata refresh refactor, that was eight points. And the initial IAM role hierarchy work, that was three points, partially done."
        },
        {
          "meeting_id": "A55CCD",
          "quote": "Okay so — three big themes for Q2. First is JIT provisioning and SCIM improvements, second is adaptive MFA policies, and third is what I'm calling the Identity audit trail, which ties into the Comply integration story."
        },
        {
          "meeting_id": "D2AE7F",
          "quote": "Phase one is directory sync and SSO configuration — basically getting Aegis Identity talking to your Entra ID environment, setting up the SAML or OIDC connectors, depending on what your apps support."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "SIEM Integration and Alert Latency",
      "definition": "Calls addressing technical issues, dropped event buffers, or significant latency when forwarding Aegis Detect telemetry to external SIEM systems like LogVault.",
      "distinguishing": "Focuses specifically on the connector/forwarding bridge and latency between Aegis Detect and third-party SIEMs, rather than total platform-wide ingestion outages.",
      "owner": "engineering lead",
      "actionable_because": "Engineering leads will fix connector buffer retry logic on network timeouts and resolve tenant processing queue imbalances.",
      "meeting_ids": [
        "24624D",
        "3DA9C2",
        "670E6D",
        "EFB1A6"
      ],
      "evidence": [
        {
          "meeting_id": "3DA9C2",
          "quote": "Okay so here's what I think is happening — in connector version 3.4.1, there's a known issue where if the HEC endpoint returns a connection timeout, specifically due to upstream throttling from something like an F5, the connector's retry logic doesn't kick in correctly, it treats the timeout as a terminal error rather than a transient one, and it flushes the buffer."
        },
        {
          "meeting_id": "670E6D",
          "quote": "The events are hitting LogVault with the correct original timestamps, but the Aegis alert notification — the one our security team acts on — that's the thing that's delayed."
        },
        {
          "meeting_id": "EFB1A6",
          "quote": "First one is expanded SIEM integration — we're adding native connectors for a couple of the major SIEM platforms in Q2, which I know you're running LogVault, so that should reduce the time from event to alert in your existing workflow."
        }
      ]
    }
